1. [input.md:9,13 | public/game.js:123-142, 223 | public/world.js:10-12, 148-156] Interacting with the `layout` map marker (`PLACES[0]` at `x: 258, y: -18`) via canvas click or `E` after `state.opened` or during `state.epilogue.packing` calls `layoutEditor()` directly instead of `layoutChoice()`. While `#task-layout` and talking to Bea route through `layoutChoice()` (which branches on `state.epilogue.packing` and `state.opened` at `public/game.js:118-119`), `interact()` at `public/game.js:223` calls `state.greeted ? layoutEditor() : layoutChoice()`. When `state.opened` is `true`, `layoutEditor()` renders all 40 `.grid-cell` buttons as `disabled`, still displays `Table`, `Seats`, and `Sound` on the grid even after Bea folded the seats and loans were returned/hidden on the canvas (`public/world.js:149`), leaves `.tool-picker` buttons (`#tool-table`, `#tool-seats`, `#tool-speaker`) and `#change-plan` enabled, and displays active placement instructions (`"Choose a supply, then choose a space. You can move it again."` / `"Placing table..."`) on an unclickable grid.
   Concrete fix: Change `public/game.js:124` from `if (!state.layout) return layoutChoice();` to `if (!state.layout || state.opened) return layoutChoice();` (or route `object.id === 'layout'` in `public/game.js:223` to `layoutChoice()` when `state.opened` is `true`).

2. [input.md:13 | public/game.js:33-39, 86, 121, 141, 175, 197-198, 207, 210, 216-217] Modal-to-modal view transitions drop keyboard focus outside the dialog to `document.body`. In `show(html)` (`public/game.js:33-38`), `const focused = modal.open ? document.activeElement?.id : null;` captures the active button ID before `body.innerHTML = html` replaces the DOM. Because `modal.open` is already `true`, `modal.showModal()` is not called, and when transitioning between distinct modal views (`photoConsent` `#take-keepsake` -> `viewKeepsake` at line 86; `journal` `#journal-keepsake` -> `viewKeepsake` at line 198; `finale` `#finale-notes` -> `journal` at lines 207/210; `journal` -> `history`/`mapInfo` at line 197; `layoutChoice` <-> `layoutEditor` at lines 121/141; `talk('celeste')` -> `muralEditor` at line 175; `showSettings` <-> `#restart` confirmation at lines 216-217), `document.getElementById(focused)` is `null`, leaving nothing focused inside `#modal`.
   Concrete fix: In `public/game.js:37`, fall back to the first focusable control inside the modal when `#${focused}` is not present: `(document.getElementById(focused) || body.querySelector('button, [href], input'))?.focus({ preventScroll: true });`.

3. [input.md:7-9,13 | public/core.js:75, 110 | public/game.js:170] Packing overwrites `photo.status === 'unasked'` to `'skipped'` (`public/core.js:75, 110`), and Rook's post-return dialogue (`public/game.js:170`) unconditionally says: `“Speaker’s home. And thanks for asking before the picture. Good company doesn’t need a camera.”` If the player goes straight to packing without ever opening `photoConsent()`, the player never asked Rook about a picture; conversely, if the player took a keepsake with consenting neighbors, `Good company doesn’t need a camera` still assumes the keepsake was skipped or only refers to Rook after assuming he was asked.
   Concrete fix: Update Rook's post-return line in `public/game.js:170` so it does not claim the player asked before the picture unless `photoConsent` was actually used, or phrase Rook's thanks around respecting his pace without assuming `photoConsent` was opened (e.g., branching on `state.epilogue.photo.status === 'taken'` vs not taken, or keeping `status: 'unasked'` distinct when `pack` is applied since `updateAfterglow()` at `public/game.js:74` already gates `#make-keepsake` on `!packing`).

4. [input.md:9,13 | public/game.js:182-188] Neighbor dialogue for Dez and Thanh is out of sequence once the gathering is open (`state.opened`) or packing (`state.epilogue.packing`).
   - `talk('dez')` (`public/game.js:182-185`): Because Dez owns no loan in `LOANS`, talking to Dez during `state.opened` or `state.epilogue.packing` still serves pre-gathering future-tense dialogue (`“Celeste said she might dance...”` / `“I’ll bring a quiet beat...”`) and a close button labeled `'See you at the gathering'` even after the gathering has opened or wound down.
   - `talk('thanh')` (`public/game.js:186-188`): When `state.opened && !state.epilogue.packing`, the first paragraph still reads `“The folding table’s already over there. You can borrow it as long as you promise to bring it back after everyone’s had their say.”` even though the table is already placed and the gathering is underway.
   Concrete fix: Branch `talk('dez')` and the first paragraph of `talk('thanh')` in `public/game.js:182-188` on `state.epilogue.packing` and `state.opened` so their copy and button labels match the active gathering and post-packing states.

